text+='## Code functions\n\n01 probes metadata/schema/unit contract; 02 probes index device/key definitions; 03 reads all 9497 provided point fragments, accounts for all points, dictionary units/range, timestamp/conflicts/duplicates, actual DST-day coverage, deterministic connection selection and old daily reconciliation; 04 independently verifies hashes, point conservation and all days of 3 fixed-source fragments; 05 recomputes dietary features on real qualified common dates using inherited versioned crosswalk; 06 independently verifies common key sets and all window formulas; 07 finalizes this memo, exact exits and aggregate flow. No predictive/interaction model, no causal conclusions.\n\n'
text+='## Calendar contract correction\n\nThe food-day key is an ISO YYYY-MM-DD string; initial CGM date was Arrow date32, causing a false zero common-day count. Script09 normalized only the representation to the existing W06 ISO key, rebuilt connection choice, daily tables and reconciliation from the completed full-point checkpoint. Prior provisional artifacts and their hashes are archived in data_qc/w09_cgm_point_qc_20261028/before_calendar_contract_fix. Script04b independently verifies final outputs; original04 is historical, not the final acceptance. No actual dates or glucose values were changed.\n\n## Rules and limits\n\nProvided HPP point series may already reflect source QC; removed upstream points cannot be recovered here. Unit/range: mounted HPP glucose dictionary mg/dL, 40..500, 15-minute sampling. Cover union of +/-7.5-minute acquisition-slot supports; this is coverage accounting, not glucose interpolation. Actual 23/24/25-hour Asia/Jerusalem calendar days. Operational candidate day: >=80% coverage, <=2h unsupported gap, regular15min cadence, no conflict/missing timestamp. 70/80/90% x1/2/4h sensitivity grid retained, model protocol thresholds and minimum days not globally frozen. Random masking assesses only MCAR mean precision.\n\nMultiple connections: maximize qualified common dates with W06 indexed energy-complete food days, earliest actual start, stable lexical ID. No glucose-value/effect selection, no automatic sensor-window concatenation; replacement cause not known.\n\nFood-only views unchanged. Food calendars are source logging dates, actual ingestion clock remains unvalidated. No oral/gut/clinical intersection yet; these Ns are not final model cohorts. Missing NOVA is retained as unknown and UPF bounds; no external mapping or invented point values.\n\n'
text+='## Corrected run and preserved initial failure\n\nInitial03 completed the point scan but stopped at legacy-field preflight: it expected cgm_mean, while the mounted daily table uses cgm_daily_mean. Initial03.log and03_initial_actual_exit_code=1 are preserved. Successful production build is03b_build_point_qc_legacy_fix.py, which preflights old fields before scanning and keeps a completed-scan checkpoint. Canonical03_actual_exit_code is a successful-build dependency marker;03b_actual_exit_code records the actual corrected script exit.\n\n'
